# 🚀 Hands-on Lab: Your New AI Teammates in Microsoft 365 Copilot

### Notebooks · Cowork · Skills

> **Time:** about 90 minutes · **Level:** Beginner · **No coding needed**

---

## 🎬 The Mission

Your manager just stopped by your desk:

> *"We're running a **Lunch & Learn** next Friday about AI at work. Can you pull it together? Agenda, a short deck, an invite email, the works. Oh, and make it repeatable, we'll do one every month."*

You could spend the afternoon on this. Or you could hand it to three AI teammates:

| Teammate | What it's like | What it does for you |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 📒 **Notebooks** | A research binder that can talk back | Keeps all your reference material in one place and answers questions about it |
| 🤝 **Cowork** | A colleague you can delegate to | Takes a goal, makes a plan, and produces real Word, PowerPoint and email outputs |
| 🧠 **Skills** | A recipe card for Copilot | Teaches Cowork *your* way of doing a task, so it does it the same way every time |

By the end of this lab you will have a notebook, a finished event pack and your own custom skill.

---

## ✅ Before You Start

Check you have:

- [ ] A work or school Microsoft 365 account with a **Microsoft 365 Copilot** license
- [ ] **Cowork** turned on for your account (if you can't see it, ask your IT admin)
- [ ] Microsoft Edge or Google Chrome
- [ ] Access to your **OneDrive**

> 💡 **Good to know**
> - Cowork uses **Copilot Credits** as it works. Keep the lab tasks small, as written.
