## 🧰 Lab 0 – Get Your Files Ready (10 min)

You need three small sample files. You'll create them yourself so everyone in the class starts with the same content.

1. Open **OneDrive** and create a folder called **`Lunch-and-Learn`**.
2. In that folder, create a **Word document** called **`Event Brief`** and paste this text:

   ```text
   EVENT BRIEF – AI at Work Lunch & Learn
   Date: Next Friday, 12:30–13:30
   Format: Hybrid (meeting room 4 + Teams)
   Audience: All staff, mostly non-technical
   Goal: Show 3 practical ways to use Copilot in daily work
   Speakers: Priya (Notebooks), Daniel (Cowork), You (Skills)
   Catering: Sandwiches and fruit for 30 people
   Budget: 400 USD
   Must include: a 10-minute Q&A and a short feedback survey
   ```

3. Create a second Word document called **`Last Session Feedback`** and paste this:

   ```text
   FEEDBACK FROM LAST LUNCH & LEARN (Excel tips)
   - "Loved the live demos, more of those please!"
   - "Slides had too much text."
   - "Started 10 minutes late, I had to leave before Q&A."
   - "Would like a one-page cheat sheet to take away."
   - "Food ran out early."
   - "Great energy from the speakers."
   ```

4. Create an **Excel workbook** called **`Budget`** with these columns and rows:

   | Item | Cost (USD) |
   | --- | --- |
   | Catering | 260 |
   | Printed cheat sheets | 40 |
   | Prizes for quiz | 60 |
   | Room AV support | 0 |

✅ **Checkpoint:** you have one folder containing three files.

