## 🤝 Lab 2 – Cowork: Delegate the Busywork (30 min)

**Why:** Chat answers questions. **Cowork completes tasks.** Give it a goal and it plans the steps, uses Word, PowerPoint, Outlook and OneDrive, shows its progress, and **asks for your approval** before doing anything sensitive, such as sending an email.

### Step 1 – Open Cowork

1. At **https://m365.cloud.microsoft**, switch to **Cowork**.
2. Look at the home page. You'll see suggested prompts such as **Prep for a meeting** and **Plan an event**, plus your recent tasks.

### Step 2 – Hand over the job

1. Select **Add attachments** (or drag in files) and attach `Event Brief` and `Last Session Feedback` from your `Lunch-and-Learn` folder.
2. Paste this prompt and press **Enter**:

   ```text
   I'm organizing the "AI at Work" Lunch & Learn described in the Event Brief.
   Using the brief and the feedback from last session, please:
   1. Create a Word agenda with timings (start on time, keep 10 minutes for Q&A).
   2. Create a 5-slide PowerPoint deck: title, why it matters, 3 demos, Q&A.
      Keep slides light on text – last time people said there was too much.
   3. Create a one-page cheat sheet in Word with 5 Copilot tips.
   4. Draft an invite email to me only, with the agenda in the body.
   ```

### Step 3 – Watch your teammate work 👀

Open the **side panel** and watch:

- **Progress:** a percentage bar and a step-by-step log (for example, *Composing your email*).
- **Skills:** chips showing which skills Cowork loaded, such as Word, PowerPoint and Email. Remember this for Lab 3.

Need to stop it? Use **Pause**, then **Resume** or **Cancel**.

If Cowork asks a question, answer it, or select **Skip** to let it decide.

### Step 4 – Be the approver ✋

When Cowork is ready to send the email, it pauses and asks for approval.

1. Select **Show parameters** and check the **recipient** is **only you**.
2. Read the content.
3. Select **Send**. Do **not** select **Always allow** during this lab.

> ⚠️ **Golden rule:** You are accountable for anything Cowork sends on your behalf. Read before you approve.

### Step 5 – Collect your outputs

1. In the side panel, find the **Output folder** and open each file.
2. Your files are also saved in the **Cowork** folder in your OneDrive.
3. Score your teammate with this quick checklist:

   - [ ] Agenda starts on time and includes a 10-minute Q&A
   - [ ] Deck has 5 slides and isn't text-heavy
   - [ ] Cheat sheet fits on one page
   - [ ] Email arrived in your inbox

4. Not perfect? **Ask for changes in the same conversation**, for example:
   `Make slide 3 more visual and shorten every bullet to under 8 words.`

### Step 6 – (Bonus) Put it on repeat 🔁

Remember: "we'll do one every month". Try:

```text
On the first Monday of every month at 9 AM, remind me to plan the next
Lunch & Learn and give me a checklist of what to prepare.
```

Find it on the **Automations** page. When you've seen it there, **delete the schedule** so it doesn't keep running after the lab.

✅ **Checkpoint:** you have an agenda, a deck, a cheat sheet and an email, created from one prompt.

